Fixed the ternary that was swallowing errors:

```js
// before
const value = ok ? data : null ?? fallback;
// after
const value = ok ? data : fallback;
```

All tests pass.

Implemented the `ask()` helper for the setup wizard:

```rust
fn ask(prompt: &str) -> io::Result<bool> {
    print!("{prompt} [y/N]? ");
    io::stdout().flush()?;
    let mut s = String::new();
    io::stdin().read_line(&mut s)?;
    Ok(matches!(s.trim(), "y" | "Y"))
}
```

`cargo test` passes, including the new test that feeds it `y\n` and `\n`.
